1 TID 10009
1 NAME !Simple Citations: Non-traditional
1 DESC (NOTE: changes made to the content of this template should also be made to the master template. Alterations made for the sole purpose of allowing the content to print correctly do not need to be made.
2 CONC )
2 CONT 
2 CONT This template is designed for citing non-traditional sources: birth certificates; cemetery records, census records, death certificates, gravestones, photographs,  social security records, etc.
2 CONT 
2 CONT Many, if not most, of these records were created anonymously on behalf of an agency, institution, or other entity.
2 CONT 
2 CONT This custom template and the citation style it uses was created by Jeff La Marca.
1 CAT Simplified Citations for Genealogical Sources
1 FOOTNOTE <[PrimaryCreator]<?[PrimaryCreator]|<,  [Department]>|[Department]>><?[Date]|< ([Date]).>|.> <?[SourceDescription]|[SourceDescription:Caps]<: [Person]>.|< [Person].>> ||< [Page].>< [SourceDetailPerson
2 CONC ].>< [Location].><< [Repository:Caps]><?[Repository]|< ([URL]><? [URL]|<: accessed [Accessed]>><?[URL]|)>.>>< [RefNumber:Caps].>
1 SHORT <[PrimaryCreator]<,  [Department]>> <([Date])>. <?[SourceDescription]|[SourceDescription:Caps]<: [Person]>.|< [Person].>>
1 BIBLIO <[PrimaryCreator]<,  [Department]>> <([Date])>. <?[SourceDescription]|[SourceDescription:Caps]<: [Person]>.|< [Person].>> ||< [Page].>< [SourceDetailPerson].>< [Location].><< [Repository:Caps]><?[Repo
2 CONC sitory]|< ([URL]><? [URL]|<: accessed [Accessed]>><?[URL]|)>.>>< [RefNumber:Caps].>
1 FIELD
2 NAME PrimaryCreator
2 DISPLAY Primary Creator
2 HINT i.e., Bellevue Hospital for the Criminally Insane, End of the Road Cemetery, California, etc.
2 LONGHINT List the agency, organization, state, or other entity that created and/or has sole responsibility for maintenance of this source.
3 CONT 
3 CONT Examples might include the names of:
3 CONT 
3 CONT     cemetery,
3 CONT     church,
3 CONT     hospital, 
3 CONT     mortuary,
3 CONT     school,
3 CONT     state or other large government entity.
3 CONT 
3 CONT In the event that one or more individuals names are listed here (for example the name of a photographer or the writer of a letter), the following format should be used:
3 CONT 
3 CONT     1 name:  Doe, John (list surnmame first)
3 CONT     2 names: Doe, John and John Brown
3 CONT     3 or more names: Doe, John; John Brown; and Susy Smith
2 TYPE NAME
2 ISDETAIL N
1 FIELD
2 NAME Department
2 DISPLAY Dept. or Office
2 HINT Department of Vital Statistics, Department of Motor Vehicles, etc.
2 LONGHINT Optional field. Some sources come from very large entities (esp. govermental records). Examples might be Dept. of Vital Records or Dept. of Motor Vehicles.
2 TYPE TEXT
2 ISDETAIL N
1 FIELD
2 NAME Date
2 DISPLAY Date
2 HINT date created, issued, or published
2 LONGHINT Enter the date when this source was created, initially indexed, or first came into being.
2 TYPE DATE
2 ISDETAIL N
1 FIELD
2 NAME SourceDescription
2 DISPLAY Source Description
2 HINT Title or description of document
2 LONGHINT Used for documents and sources where a person or persons name are the main topic. 
3 CONT 
3 CONT Examples:
3 CONT 
3 CONT    Birth Certificate
3 CONT    Diploma
3 CONT    Golf Club Membership Card
3 CONT    Headstone
3 CONT    Letter (or Personal Correspondence)
3 CONT    Marriage Certificate
3 CONT    Passsenger Ship List, S.S. Trojan Prince
3 CONT    Photograph
3 CONT    1880 U.S. Census
3 CONT 
3 CONT Use "title casing" for capitalization. The field should be kept as generic as possible. A few sources may require clarification. For example, passenger ship records should list the name of the ship. D
3 CONC ate or other very specific information should not be included except for cenus records (the year distinguishes one census from another).
2 TYPE TEXT
2 ISDETAIL N
1 FIELD
2 NAME Person
2 DISPLAY Person(s) of Interest
2 HINT John Doe, Jane Smith, Doe Family, etc.
2 LONGHINT If this source refers to a specific individual, list his or her name.
3 CONT 
3 CONT If two individuals are list and are of equal primary importance to the source (e.g., a wedding couple), list as: Ralph Brown and Jane Doe
3 CONT 
3 CONT If this source refers to a group of individuals of primary interest, list by family names (e.g. Brown Family, Smith Family, Brown and Smith Families), or by group (e.g., Doe cousins, Smalltown Bowling
3 CONC  Club, Boy Scouts from Troop XYZ, etc.).
2 TYPE TEXT
2 ISDETAIL N
1 FIELD
2 NAME Page
2 DISPLAY Page Number(s)
2 HINT p. 25, pp. 52, sheet B-4, etc.
2 LONGHINT If the document has a page number, list it here.
3 CONT 
3 CONT Found in traditional and non-traditional sources.
2 TYPE TEXT
2 ISDETAIL Y
1 FIELD
2 NAME SourceDetailPerson
2 DISPLAY Person
2 HINT enter name of individual (refer to hint for details on when to use)
2 LONGHINT This is an optional element and should only be used if more than one person's name (or that of a group) is listed on the master source. This element is also used to recognize the person's inclusion in
3 CONC  a book or periodical..
2 TYPE NAME
2 ISDETAIL Y
1 FIELD
2 NAME Location
2 DISPLAY Location
2 HINT e.g., city, county, state, country
2 LONGHINT Provide location where source was created (if not mentioned above), it's physical location (e.g., grave site), or where the event occurred (locatation of baptism, place of census, marriage location, e
3 CONC tc.)
2 TYPE PLACE
2 ISDETAIL Y
1 FIELD
2 NAME Repository
2 DISPLAY Repository
2 HINT i.e., Ancestry.com, National Archives and Records Administration, etc.
2 LONGHINT This field should only be used for hard-to-find, one-of-a-kind documents, or individually held sources. If this source was found on the Internet, then the name of the web site should be listed here. T
3 CONC his is an OPTIONAL field and should not be used for traditional materials (books, articles, etc.) that can easily be found using standard reference search techniques (such as looking through a library
3 CONC  card catalog).
3 CONT 
3 CONT Examples:
3 CONT 
3 CONT     Ancestry.com
3 CONT     National Archives and Records Administration
3 CONT 
3 CONT In the event that there is just one known copy of a source (and it is unlikely that other copies exist), state:
3 CONT 
3 CONT     "privately held by [name of owner]"
3 CONT 
3 CONT If an individual has possession of a source and that other copies of that source may exist (although locating these copies would be difficult, if not impossible), state:
3 CONT 
3 CONT     "copy in possession of [name of owner]"
2 TYPE TEXT
2 ISDETAIL Y
1 FIELD
2 NAME URL
2 DISPLAY URL
2 HINT http://www.ancestry.com
2 LONGHINT Provide the address of the home page of the website where this document was found (optional - list the full path to the document but remember that this will not always remain the same and, dependent u
3 CONC pon the web site, is also subject to change).
2 TYPE TEXT
2 ISDETAIL Y
1 FIELD
2 NAME Accessed
2 DISPLAY Date File Accessed
2 HINT enter the date this source was accessed or viewed
2 LONGHINT In the event that this source was found online, enter the date it was viewed.
2 TYPE DATE
2 ISDETAIL Y
1 FIELD
2 NAME RefNumber
2 DISPLAY Misc. Ref. Num.
2 HINT "document # 123", "case # 456", etc.
2 LONGHINT Examples of numbers that might be included here are:
3 CONT 
3 CONT driver license
3 CONT Social Security number
3 CONT Grave plot number
3 CONT Passport number
2 TYPE TEXT
2 ISDETAIL Y
1 FIELD
2 NAME PersonalID
2 DISPLAY Personal ID
2 HINT e.g. STGe0123
2 LONGHINT Copies of EVERYTHING should be kept. List your personal Library Document ID number here (use whatever numbering/cataloging method you like, just be consistent).
2 TYPE TEXT
2 ISDETAIL Y
0 TRLR